    "narrative": "As we navigate the tail end of the 2026 campaign, the Austin Waves roster remains heavily impacted by the league schedule, with heavy hitters like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** inactive today. This forces a reliance on our depth, where **Liam Hicks** stands as our strongest play with a 50.13 score. Despite the \"Lineup Pending\" tag, his projected cleanup spot against Shawn Armstrong (4.35 xERA) provides a solid floor. The 11% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage against right-handed pitching outweighs the minor park factor penalty, making him the focal point of our offensive production for this slate.\n\nRegarding the lower end of the lineup, **Brayan Rocchio** narrowly scraped into the starting spot with a 40.89 score. While he faces Freddy Peralta\u2014an arm who requires caution despite a middling 4.32 xERA\u2014**Brayan Rocchio** earns the start primarily due to the lack of viable alternatives on our bench. The optimizer penalized him for his likely #9 spot in the order, which suppresses his RBI and run-scoring upside. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL; his absence continues to be a primary drag on our stolen base efficiency, a category where we desperately need high-sprint-speed contributors like him or the prospects in our pipeline to eventually solidify the bottom half of the roster.",
